<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!--
      Deliberately no INTERNET permission here: this is the release
      manifest, and the app's core privacy claim is that it never requests
      network access. Metro's dev-server permission lives ONLY in
      src/debug/AndroidManifest.xml, merged into debug builds, never release.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.CAMERA" />

    <application
      android:name=".MainApplication"
      android:label="@string/app_name"
      android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
      android:roundIcon="@mipmap/ic_launcher_round"
      android:allowBackup="false"
      android:theme="@style/AppTheme"
      android:usesCleartextTraffic="${usesCleartextTraffic}"
      android:supportsRtl="true">
      <!--
        libOpenCL.so access is deliberately NOT declared here; CPU-only
        fallback is the safe default until the GPU path is re-verified (see
        below).

        HISTORY: first tried on 2026-08-16 with a Snapdragon 778G+ / Adreno
        642L device (this project's other test phone, an A6x-class GPU).
        libOpenCL.so loaded, but llama.rn's OpenCL backend registration then
        called ggml_abort(), a hard SIGABRT crash, not a graceful fallback,
        because that GPU isn't in its supported tier, a real, confirmed,
        unaddressed risk for any device outside the verified support tier,
        since this is a single shared manifest with no runtime chip-tier
        detection. Reverted, then re-enabled on 2026-08-16 specifically to
        test a Nothing Phone (3) (Snapdragon 8s Gen 4 / SM8735, Adreno 825)
        which worked perfectly for hours: 18.8s extractions, exact-match
        accuracy.

        2026-08-17: on that same Nothing Phone 3, extraction started
        failing with empty/hallucinated output (not a crash). At the time
        this was suspected to be OpenCL backend degradation and "fixed" by
        removing this declaration, but that fix was never actually
        verified, and it was the wrong theory. ROOT CAUSE, established the
        same session via `dumpsys thermalservice`: severe SoC thermal
        throttling (Thermal Status SEVERE, CPU cores 79.6-99.9C) from
        sustained back-to-back extractions, corroborated by an emulator
        control comparison (CPU-only, no OpenCL involved at all) producing
        the correct result once thermally unconstrained. See CLAUDE.md's
        mobile caveat section for the full evidence chain.

        2026-08-24 re-verification: same phone, now cooled (live sensors
        34-53C during the run, Thermal Status LIGHT at most), same code,
        still WITHOUT this declaration (CPU-only fallback); extraction
        succeeded with an exact-match result. This confirms heat was the
        real cause, but does NOT tell us whether OpenCL registration itself
        was ever actually degraded, since the GPU path wasn't re-tested.
        Left disabled here rather than restored: re-enabling the
        accelerated path needs its own deliberate re-test on cooled
        hardware with thermals monitored throughout, given the confirmed
        778G+ crash risk this manifest still carries either way.
      -->
      <activity
        android:name=".MainActivity"
        android:label="@string/app_name"
        android:configChanges="keyboard|keyboardHidden|orientation|screenLayout|screenSize|smallestScreenSize|uiMode"
        android:launchMode="singleTask"
        android:windowSoftInputMode="adjustResize"
        android:exported="true">
        <intent-filter>
            <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
            <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
        </intent-filter>
      </activity>
    </application>
</manifest>
